<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isbn> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "International Standard Book Number (ISBN) <https://www.isbn-international.org/content/isbn-users-manual/29> is a unique numeric identifier for monographic publications standardized by ISO 2108 <https://www.iso.org/standard/65483.html>. It consists of either 10 digits (for assignments prior to January 1, 2007) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISBN is composed of five parts: a GS1 prefix, a registration group, a registrant, a publication element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., 9780198836063)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/startTime> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A timestamp marking the commencement of an action,\nthe beginning of an element's relevance,\nor the intended start of either.\n\nIt encompasses the moment of triggering processes,\nsuch as build executions or service instantiations,\nas well as the point in time when an element\nor a relationship between elements becomes effective or active."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Core/RelationshipType/verifiedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "verifiedBy"@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/Build/buildId> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A buildId is a locally unique identifier used by a builder to identify a unique\ninstance of a build produced by it."@en .
