<https://spdx.org/rdf/3/terms/SupplyChain/State> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A state is an instance that describes what a system, component, subsystem, process, or project has achieved at any given time. States are used to describe different conditions within a system and provide information about its current status. They help us understand the behavior of systems or product by showing their progression through various states over time.\n\nStates describe what a project has achieved (or not) as opposed to describing actions taken by people involved with the project, or activities performed during development of that project."@en .
